fb2c75ca-ce97-46d3-ac70-c3e486a37659	2026-09-15 17:23:16.691916+00	2026-09-15 17:23:16.692535+00	16	16	VERTICAL LIVING GARDENS At the heart of the design are vertical living gardensΓÇöa sequence of terraced green platforms that gradually rise from street level to the podium. These terraces shape outdoor rooms for everyday use: shaded courtyards, open lawns, gathering pavilions, and wellness spaces. Planting is layered and staggered to raise the overall ΓÇ£green volume,ΓÇ¥ ensuring that greenery surrounds the built form from multiple levels and viewpoints. NATURE-CENTRIC LEARNING & ECOLOGICAL STEWARDSHIP A key feature of the landscape is its nature-centric learning environment, built around the idea of ecological stewardship. At its centre lies a Miyawaki mini forest that preserves biodiversity while creating immersive nature experiences. Re∩¼éexology trails, sensory gardens, and play areas allow residentsΓÇöespecially childrenΓÇöto explore and interact with the natural environment. This space becomes a living laboratory, nurturing curiosity, environmental awareness, and a deeper connection with nature within an urban setting. COMMUNITY SPACES, NATURALLY LIVED IN Community spaces here are planned as part of everyday living; not set apart from it. Amenities are distributed across the podium and carefully woven into the landscape, allowing movement, pause, and interaction to happen naturally rather than by design. There are open areas for activity and play, quieter corners for conversation or re∩¼éection, and shaded zones that remain comfortable through the day. Each space is positioned to feel intuitive, used when needed, and unobtrusive when not. These spaces donΓÇÖt ask for special occasions or planned visits. They support small, daily momentsΓÇöstepping out for fresh air, meeting a neighbour, or simply taking a pause between routines. They are not destinations. They are part of how the day unfolds. Residential Units Double height Sky Deck Gym Indoor Game Area Doubl